#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "8ea17e06-1248-510c-9e71-c57da0cb0d02" :question/math-academy-id "e-14405" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "1579f932-6e7f-5daa-b001-54a9f6c236ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14406" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "d2f49acf-ed91-510d-a0f1-41c50eeef9e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-14422" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805b84a4-d27a-514e-a586-c2d6e38ad057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid \\ln x \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098113} {:answer/id #uuid "c6443f24-a54f-599c-b46d-4a92ba5f6412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid \\ln (2x) \\mid" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098114} {:answer/id #uuid "efa53843-32a8-5214-bb83-d2fb2520dd02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid \\ln (2x) \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098115} {:answer/id #uuid "1f850e51-5bf2-56ac-be8c-d40b226c0d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid \\ln x \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098116} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5b46e7-f467-56b7-bf9d-e77d4ff0c13b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid \\ln (2x) \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e5b46e7-f467-56b7-bf9d-e77d4ff0c13b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid \\ln (2x) \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098117} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe1f0732-f569-5035-958f-d5910a218a37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe83e5e8-3e8c-5cd2-aca6-78f5c7a59344" :question/math-academy-id "q-13802" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a56840dc-5e00-5f49-b590-1f3863c348f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288891} {:answer/id #uuid "a0dedd3f-bd40-52de-9650-d627896afc09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288892} {:answer/id #uuid "889ad441-d1c4-56a6-b705-7aa5a5f2f558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288893} {:answer/id #uuid "6a605c5d-653a-5ed3-ad3c-426e45c63748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288894} {:answer/id #uuid "cc76caca-bc0f-52ed-8254-97e818f1b12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "889ad441-d1c4-56a6-b705-7aa5a5f2f558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288893} :answer-field/id #uuid "291f4bbb-6be7-5dcb-b262-66285993d76d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2a8959c-6b04-5ef7-8052-da57da0ea3d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-13803" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190c27db-dd0f-559a-902b-5dbc83d859ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288898} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ac7ac3-d198-554a-9743-ea0f4f9b7c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288899} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f8db47-fddc-5cd3-b5b6-2928fd2958fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288900} {:answer/id #uuid "473cdab0-4256-5c6c-a43c-0f4779694bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288901} {:answer/id #uuid "fd704b15-f081-5cf0-858c-24b42eb59cc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "190c27db-dd0f-559a-902b-5dbc83d859ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288898} :answer-field/id #uuid "84906a4b-b873-5500-8bf5-b8c633338e14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4234ecef-6101-5408-8e19-a789f906baa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-13807" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}\\cdot  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d1829b6-226a-59cc-ac84-7f70965b07ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288905} {:answer/id #uuid "034d5368-5634-501b-8b12-5d08897bafb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288906} {:answer/id #uuid "07324f29-5966-586d-9fb8-528de2658edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288907} {:answer/id #uuid "9566a656-778f-5411-9730-91f0f85885d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288908} {:answer/id #uuid "9113c0d7-8669-5745-b3db-515179197b98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9566a656-778f-5411-9730-91f0f85885d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288908} :answer-field/id #uuid "45cdad24-554c-585e-951c-83c395fde969" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25f19f3c-0b42-5a9e-a3d7-4998abc0a9b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-13845" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $e/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{e/4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{1}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0af3f528-1cd9-5154-9953-7c5f5220b388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288912} {:answer/id #uuid "0f658357-6ee5-551b-b3fd-38bef5ec88fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288913} {:answer/id #uuid "cca61265-4745-506b-a432-d69629bfe22d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{ln}^{3}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288914} {:answer/id #uuid "1b9682a4-d6f2-5bbf-a441-a51971d11256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{ln}^{3}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288915} {:answer/id #uuid "b9645792-77d0-50d3-a187-14af57110cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9645792-77d0-50d3-a187-14af57110cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288916} :answer-field/id #uuid "15151c10-adea-5fb3-952b-343a131260dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e134589-c376-59bd-843a-f5bacb6308a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-210742" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}\\cdot  \\\\  & =6\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+C \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b8263f6-0eec-5b6c-8617-0ca7d6c2ac71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288919} {:answer/id #uuid "de0b956b-1133-5f24-8e0a-a5e4499c624f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288920} {:answer/id #uuid "b64ceb84-429c-5862-af05-a51823f63ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288921} {:answer/id #uuid "0628a5ef-9e65-5719-8bf9-6b4e90596f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288922} {:answer/id #uuid "427867e6-0a7c-55e6-bf02-2fd67e867f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de0b956b-1133-5f24-8e0a-a5e4499c624f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288920} :answer-field/id #uuid "d43a5979-cea6-574c-8eef-3102737d664e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1ac204a3-c26a-5153-94fe-5a9acfd15332" :question/math-academy-id "q-210781" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡(2x).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{3}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡(2x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81c36c65-35ca-5d52-a03d-92482fb6b1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099339} {:answer/id #uuid "ef822792-3cf4-5a17-86ee-bb3dbb4f35a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln x \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099340} {:answer/id #uuid "f225c7a5-c416-5406-a430-71fcc48bcc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099341} {:answer/id #uuid "127c18f7-2532-52ea-bf09-7ea32a936b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln x \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{x} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099342} {:answer/id #uuid "399c3e46-e63f-548b-ad88-0cb54e0a6e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 3 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f225c7a5-c416-5406-a430-71fcc48bcc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\log_{2}^{2} x}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099341} :answer-field/id #uuid "4456b3bc-a2cb-5663-9041-ec22b84552ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc1950d7-cc9c-5e9a-8f86-5dcc05de2e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-31329" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd13c43-9507-5941-86aa-5411c48ed808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288926} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f3c4e1-90a5-55d9-8b37-bec463cfa521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288927} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0bfd8a-1337-5353-9115-afd616cf4dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288928} {:answer/id #uuid "9d776e92-57ee-56b1-a88d-9435df509800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288929} {:answer/id #uuid "76fd98a9-5f72-5ada-af96-9f5e50a16e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc0bfd8a-1337-5353-9115-afd616cf4dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288928} :answer-field/id #uuid "65594974-9339-5cbb-aaea-daf806666fb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7d778489-5860-55d0-a860-26c713534ade" :question/math-academy-id "q-31397" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{log}_{3}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{3}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be226d19-d6c8-5673-8d15-e0a5b50957e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288933} {:answer/id #uuid "00ebc433-672a-5713-b1b6-f956bacdc5a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288934} {:answer/id #uuid "feb6fcbd-3a3c-5da8-bc3e-f6194d6eac40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288935} {:answer/id #uuid "c8d00600-d79e-5010-8a77-6cd62efd0f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288936} {:answer/id #uuid "039b7f02-889f-54bf-b89c-366effd8a329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}{ln}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feb6fcbd-3a3c-5da8-bc3e-f6194d6eac40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288935} :answer-field/id #uuid "82c9f2b6-bdfc-5d52-832e-d800c88d82fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dd1d32f-b149-5f3f-b3a9-56bf64944e84" :question/math-academy-id "q-31398" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{ln}^{3}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecf8598e-6eea-5703-9c31-ff8196baf45d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288940} {:answer/id #uuid "243a3bd8-64e9-5a14-82ca-22d97fda1b37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288941} {:answer/id #uuid "e2247c3f-e755-57a0-ae66-bfdfc706cc1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288942} {:answer/id #uuid "fae7eb33-6046-5f29-b1b7-5e65446b8fad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288943} {:answer/id #uuid "48938fcd-ea07-58eb-956b-7b982f09e7b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48938fcd-ea07-58eb-956b-7b982f09e7b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288944} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac3879c7-cbb1-5376-b8fc-d1131727dee1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c53474e-e877-5764-b2e1-1623184bc76e" :question/math-academy-id "q-31400" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dd90c1c-26ec-5941-9014-a75801549c55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x\\log_{3}^{2} x}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099347} {:answer/id #uuid "a0694e18-a828-5c4b-ba1a-9eb0be4df438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\ln 3\\log_{3}^{2} (x^{2}))/(4) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099348} {:answer/id #uuid "a418d3da-146c-5dfa-9623-7d22db2c2bb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\ln 3\\log_{3}^{2} (x^{2}))/(2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099349} {:answer/id #uuid "182c11c5-a79d-57e1-a63e-bcd27e737eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\ln 2\\log_{2}^{2} (x^{2}))/(4) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099350} {:answer/id #uuid "64858e3a-933f-5c31-a6dd-383d968fac37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\ln (x^{2})\\log_{3}^{2} (x^{2}))/(2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0694e18-a828-5c4b-ba1a-9eb0be4df438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\ln 3\\log_{3}^{2} (x^{2}))/(4) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099348} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a92435-e746-5ef5-af8a-b64dd53759d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8e9ea16-ddaf-5f82-ac82-079325b04f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31401" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}).$Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\int u\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e673357c-b410-5f96-9b33-c8b4ccf787e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e673357c-b410-5f96-9b33-c8b4ccf787e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{75}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288947} :answer-field/id #uuid "b522b96f-b6f0-580b-98ff-2190e85faf4b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b56979c-6ffd-5144-983e-db25c6dde3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-346434" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot {u}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}({4}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =\\frac{75}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91355321-4aaa-5827-b25a-f768637dd369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91355321-4aaa-5827-b25a-f768637dd369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288950} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a5ec03-5b0e-5ce0-ae81-bcd6e12d0f3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fec3228-1358-581c-bfd2-8d4b419af6b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-346435" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $32$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{u}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f7750a3-cd87-50af-ac0e-8c6db22ccbb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288953} {:answer/id #uuid "c565f3d0-1788-59c5-b844-e68b6a120590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c565f3d0-1788-59c5-b844-e68b6a120590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288954} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e408cab-5de5-5cd1-a8b9-2d7cdb3b8d0d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b0fab75-92d3-57f7-aef2-4351e6b585ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-351283" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $81$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot (2\\sqrt{u}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3(2-1) \\\\  & =(4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d4e914-777e-5d39-bff5-e6c1b095c7b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\ln(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08d4e914-777e-5d39-bff5-e6c1b095c7b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\ln(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288957} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc41768-8fe2-54d7-8499-5395b932e732" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7bb151c-aa2a-5b17-87e8-0a807a1157b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-351287" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $125$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
